---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Tracepod — Container hardening based on what your workloads actually do"
  description="Tracepod profiles running container workloads via eBPF and produces minimised OCI images, seccomp allowlists, AppArmor profiles, and signed SBOMs — all grounded in observed runtime behaviour."
>

  <!-- ============================================================
       HERO
       ============================================================ -->
  <section class="hero section">
    <div class="container hero-inner">
      <div class="hero-content">
        <div class="eyebrow">Open-core &middot; AGPL-3.0 &middot; Kubernetes-native</div>
        <h1 class="heading-xl hero-headline">
          Harden containers based on what they actually do
          <span class="headline-accent"> at runtime.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="body-lg hero-sub">
          Tracepod attaches an eBPF sensor to your running workloads, captures every file they touch,
          and produces a minimised OCI image, seccomp allowlist, AppArmor profile, and signed SBOM &mdash;
          automatically. Attack surface you can measure, not guess.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a href="/docs/getting-started/quickstart/" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">
            Get started free
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
          </a>
          <a href="/platform" class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg">See the platform</a>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-badges">
          <span class="badge">
            <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 2L3 7v6c0 5.5 3.8 10.7 9 12 5.2-1.3 9-6.5 9-12V7L12 2z"/></svg>
            eBPF-powered
          </span>
          <span class="badge">CycloneDX + SPDX SBOMs</span>
          <span class="badge">cosign-signed</span>
          <span class="badge">CO-RE (no kernel module)</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-terminal" aria-label="Quickstart example">
        <div class="terminal">
          <div class="terminal-bar">
            <div class="terminal-dot"></div>
            <div class="terminal-dot"></div>
            <div class="terminal-dot"></div>
            <span class="terminal-title">bash</span>
          </div>
          <div class="terminal-body">
            <p><span class="comment"># Install via Helm</span></p>
            <p><span class="prompt">$</span> helm repo add tracepod https://charts.tracepod.co.uk</p>
            <p><span class="prompt">$</span> helm install tracepod tracepod/tracepod \</p>
            <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;--namespace tracepod --create-namespace</p>
            <p>&nbsp;</p>
            <p><span class="comment"># Profile a workload for 60 s, then harden</span></p>
            <p><span class="prompt">$</span> <span class="cmd">tracepod</span> profile --workload nginx/my-app --duration 60s</p>
            <p><span class="output">&nbsp;&nbsp;&#8627; Profiling my-app (nginx:1.25.3)&hellip;</span></p>
            <p><span class="output">&nbsp;&nbsp;&#8627; Observed 847 unique file paths</span></p>
            <p>&nbsp;</p>
            <p><span class="prompt">$</span> <span class="cmd">tracepod</span> harden --workload nginx/my-app \</p>
            <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;--push registry.example.com/my-app:hardened</p>
            <p><span class="success">&nbsp;&nbsp;&#10003; Image size:&nbsp; 248 MB &rarr; 31 MB (87% smaller)</span></p>
            <p><span class="success">&nbsp;&nbsp;&#10003; CVEs:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;142 &rarr; 9 (grype, CRITICAL/HIGH)</span></p>
            <p><span class="success">&nbsp;&nbsp;&#10003; Syscalls:&nbsp;&nbsp; 386 &rarr; 58 (seccomp allowlist)</span></p>
            <p><span class="success">&nbsp;&nbsp;&#10003; SBOM signed and pushed alongside image</span></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================================
       LOOP DIAGRAM
       ============================================================ -->
  <section class="loop-section section--tight">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div class="eyebrow">How it works</div>
        <h2 class="heading-lg">Four outputs from one profiling run</h2>
        <p class="body-md section-sub">
          A single eBPF sensor session produces a complete hardening bundle &mdash; no guesswork, no allow-all defaults.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="loop-diagram">
        <div class="loop-step">
          <div class="loop-step-icon">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true">
              <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/>
              <path d="M12 1v4M12 19v4M4.22 4.22l2.83 2.83M16.95 16.95l2.83 2.83M1 12h4M19 12h4M4.22 19.78l2.83-2.83M16.95 7.05l2.83-2.83"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="loop-step-num label">01</div>
          <h3 class="loop-step-title">Profile</h3>
          <p class="loop-step-body">eBPF sensor attaches to running containers via kprobes, capturing every <code>openat()</code> syscall &mdash; filtered by cgroup/namespace, zero kernel module required.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="loop-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        </div>

        <div class="loop-step">
          <div class="loop-step-icon">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true">
              <rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/>
              <path d="M9 9h6M9 12h6M9 15h4"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="loop-step-num label">02</div>
          <h3 class="loop-step-title">Minimise</h3>
          <p class="loop-step-body">Only observed files &mdash; plus recursively resolved ELF shared libraries and language-runtime companions &mdash; go into the new OCI image layer. Every file tagged by source.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="loop-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        </div>

        <div class="loop-step">
          <div class="loop-step-icon">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="loop-step-num label">03</div>
          <h3 class="loop-step-title">Harden</h3>
          <p class="loop-step-body">Generate a seccomp syscall allowlist and AppArmor profile directly from observed runtime behaviour &mdash; precise, not over-permissive.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="loop-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        </div>

        <div class="loop-step">
          <div class="loop-step-icon">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/>
              <polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/>
              <path d="M9 13h6M9 17h4"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="loop-step-num label">04</div>
          <h3 class="loop-step-title">Sign &amp; attest</h3>
          <p class="loop-step-body">CycloneDX and SPDX SBOMs generated by syft, signed with cosign, pushed alongside the image. Auditable, portable, supply-chain ready.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================================
       CONFIDENCE SCORES
       ============================================================ -->
  <section class="confidence-section section">
    <div class="container confidence-inner">
      <div class="confidence-text">
        <div class="eyebrow">Confidence scoring</div>
        <h2 class="heading-lg">Every file carries its source &mdash; so you can trust the result.</h2>
        <p class="body-md">
          Most container-slimming tools give you a plain file list. Tracepod tags every path with the observation source:
          direct eBPF observation, inferred ELF dependency, inferred runtime companion, or manually added.
          That distinction is the foundation of confidence scoring &mdash; you see exactly what you&rsquo;re shipping and why.
        </p>
        <p class="body-md" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
          A minimised image that crashes in production is worse than not hardening at all.
          Tracepod is designed to eliminate that outcome.
        </p>
        <a href="/docs/concepts/how-profiling-works/" class="btn btn-secondary" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
          Read the concept docs
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="confidence-visual">
        <div class="terminal">
          <div class="terminal-bar">
            <div class="terminal-dot"></div>
            <div class="terminal-dot"></div>
            <div class="terminal-dot"></div>
            <span class="terminal-title">manifest.json (excerpt)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="terminal-body manifest-body">
            <pre set:html={`<span class="output">&#123;</span>
  <span class="output">"files": [</span>
    <span class="output">&#123;</span>
      <span class="output">  "path": "/usr/bin/python3.11",</span>
      <span class="success">  "source": "direct",</span>
      <span class="output">  "count": 312,</span>
      <span class="output">  "confidence": 0.99</span>
    <span class="output">&#125;,</span>
    <span class="output">&#123;</span>
      <span class="output">  "path": "/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6",</span>
      <span class="cmd">  "source": "inferred-elf",</span>
      <span class="output">  "confidence": 0.95</span>
    <span class="output">&#125;,</span>
    <span class="output">&#123;</span>
      <span class="output">  "path": "/usr/lib/python3.11/encodings/",</span>
      <span class="output">  "source": "inferred-runtime",</span>
      <span class="output">  "confidence": 0.90</span>
    <span class="output">&#125;</span>
  <span class="output">]</span>
<span class="output">&#125;</span>`}></pre>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="source-legend">
          <div class="legend-item"><span class="legend-dot direct"></span><span class="legend-label label">direct</span><span class="legend-desc">observed by eBPF</span></div>
          <div class="legend-item"><span class="legend-dot elf"></span><span class="legend-label label">inferred-elf</span><span class="legend-desc">ELF shared-lib dependency</span></div>
          <div class="legend-item"><span class="legend-dot runtime"></span><span class="legend-label label">inferred-runtime</span><span class="legend-desc">language-runtime companion</span></div>
          <div class="legend-item"><span class="legend-dot manual"></span><span class="legend-label label">manual</span><span class="legend-desc">user-added override</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================================
       OSS vs PRO
       ============================================================ -->
  <section class="compare-section section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div class="eyebrow">Open-core model</div>
        <h2 class="heading-lg">Everything you need is free and open source.<br>The platform takes it further.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="compare-grid">
        <!-- OSS column -->
        <div class="compare-col compare-col--oss">
          <div class="compare-col-header">
            <div class="label">Open Source</div>
            <div class="compare-col-badge">AGPL-3.0</div>
          </div>
          <ul class="feature-list">
            <li class="feature-item">
              <span class="feature-check">&#10003;</span>
              <div>
                <strong>eBPF sensor</strong>
                <span class="feature-desc">CO-RE kprobe sensor, ring buffer consumer, cgroup filtering</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="feature-item">
              <span class="feature-check">&#10003;</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Image builder (hardener)</strong>
                <span class="feature-desc">Minimised OCI image, ELF resolver, directory-inclusion mode</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="feature-item">
              <span class="feature-check">&#10003;</span>
              <div>
                <strong>CLI (<code>tracepod</code>)</strong>
                <span class="feature-desc">Profile, harden, push &mdash; single binary, CGO-free</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="feature-item">
              <span class="feature-check">&#10003;</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Helm chart</strong>
                <span class="feature-desc">DaemonSet + aggregation controller, RBAC, Kubernetes-native</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="feature-item">
              <span class="feature-check">&#10003;</span>
              <div>
                <strong>GitHub Action</strong>
                <span class="feature-desc">Drop-in CI hardening step, matrix kernel support</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="feature-item">
              <span class="feature-check">&#10003;</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Seccomp + AppArmor profiles</strong>
                <span class="feature-desc">Syscall allowlist and AppArmor profiles from observed behaviour</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="feature-item">
              <span class="feature-check">&#10003;</span>
              <div>
                <strong>CycloneDX + SPDX SBOMs</strong>
                <span class="feature-desc">Generated by syft, signed with cosign</span>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <a href="/open-source" class="btn btn-secondary compare-cta">View open-source tools</a>
        </div>

        <!-- Pro column -->
        <div class="compare-col compare-col--pro">
          <div class="compare-col-header">
            <div class="label">Platform</div>
            <div class="compare-col-badge compare-col-badge--pro">Pro</div>
          </div>
          <p class="compare-col-intro">Everything in open source, plus:</p>
          <ul class="feature-list">
            <li class="feature-item">
              <span class="feature-check feature-check--pro">&#10003;</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Web dashboard</strong>
                <span class="feature-desc">Fleet view of workloads, builds, validations, and compliance</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="feature-item">
              <span class="feature-check feature-check--pro">&#10003;</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Sandbox validation</strong>
                <span class="feature-desc">Run the hardened container in an ephemeral sandbox; detect missing files before you ship</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="feature-item">
              <span class="feature-check feature-check--pro">&#10003;</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Auto-fix loop</strong>
                <span class="feature-desc">Validate &rarr; rebuild with missing paths &rarr; revalidate, up to 3 rounds, unattended</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="feature-item">
              <span class="feature-check feature-check--pro">&#10003;</span>
              <div>
                <strong>CVE delta reports</strong>
                <span class="feature-desc">grype scan of source vs hardened image &mdash; exact vulnerability reduction counts</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="feature-item">
              <span class="feature-check feature-check--pro">&#10003;</span>
              <div>
                <strong>One-click apply + drift detection</strong>
                <span class="feature-desc">Patch the live workload; dashboard alerts when it drifts from the hardened ref</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="feature-item">
              <span class="feature-check feature-check--pro">&#10003;</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Fleet policy &amp; compliance</strong>
                <span class="feature-desc">Namespace-scoped policies: min coverage, hardened required, validated required</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="feature-item">
              <span class="feature-check feature-check--pro">&#10003;</span>
              <div>
                <strong>OpenVEX export with reachability</strong>
                <span class="feature-desc">Machine-readable VEX documents based on whether a vulnerable component is in the minimised image</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="feature-item">
              <span class="feature-check feature-check--pro">&#10003;</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Webhooks + source-image watching</strong>
                <span class="feature-desc">Auto-rebuild when the source image changes; push outcomes to any endpoint</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="feature-item">
              <span class="feature-check feature-check--pro">&#10003;</span>
              <div>
                <strong>RBAC + audit log</strong>
                <span class="feature-desc">Kubernetes TokenReview, role-based access, immutable audit trail</span>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary compare-cta">Contact us</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================================
       TRUST SIGNALS
       ============================================================ -->
  <section class="trust-section section--tight">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="trust-grid">
        <div class="trust-item">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" class="trust-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/>
          </svg>
          <h4>AGPL-3.0 licensed</h4>
          <p>The core toolchain is fully open. Inspect the code, run it yourself, contribute upstream.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="trust-item">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" class="trust-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/>
            <path d="M9 9h6M9 12h6M9 15h4"/>
          </svg>
          <h4>CycloneDX + SPDX SBOMs</h4>
          <p>Both formats, signed with cosign. Works with whatever your enterprise security toolchain already expects.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="trust-item">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" class="trust-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/>
            <path d="M12 8v4l3 3"/>
          </svg>
          <h4>CO-RE &mdash; no kernel module</h4>
          <p>Pure eBPF with Compile Once, Run Everywhere. Supports kernel 6.8+ without rebuilding on each node.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="trust-item">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" class="trust-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M21 16V8a2 2 0 0 0-1-1.73l-7-4a2 2 0 0 0-2 0l-7 4A2 2 0 0 0 3 8v8a2 2 0 0 0 1 1.73l7 4a2 2 0 0 0 2 0l7-4A2 2 0 0 0 21 16z"/>
          </svg>
          <h4>Kubernetes-native</h4>
          <p>DaemonSet deployment, TokenReview RBAC, existing registry secrets &mdash; no side-car injection, no admission webhook required.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================================
       FINAL CTA BAND
       ============================================================ -->
  <section class="cta-band section">
    <div class="container cta-band-inner">
      <div>
        <h2 class="heading-lg">Ready to measure your attack surface?</h2>
        <p class="body-md" style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
          Start with the open-source CLI in minutes. Talk to us about the platform.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-band-actions">
        <a href="/docs/getting-started/quickstart/" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">
          Get started free
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        </a>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg">Contact us</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
/* Hero */
.hero { padding-top: var(--space-16); }
.hero-inner {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  gap: var(--space-16);
  align-items: center;
}
.hero-content { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-6); }
.hero-headline { line-height: 1.07; }
.headline-accent { color: var(--accent); }
.hero-sub { max-width: 520px; }
.btn-lg { padding: 0.8rem 1.75rem; font-size: 1rem; }
.hero-actions { display: flex; gap: var(--space-3); flex-wrap: wrap; }
.hero-badges { display: flex; gap: var(--space-2); flex-wrap: wrap; }
.badge {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--space-1);
  padding: 0.3rem 0.7rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 999px;
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
  font-size: 0.72rem;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
}
.badge svg { color: var(--accent); }
.hero-terminal { width: 100%; }

/* Loop */
.section-header {
  text-align: center;
  max-width: 640px;
  margin: 0 auto var(--space-12);
}
.section-sub { color: var(--text-secondary); margin-top: var(--space-4); }

.loop-diagram {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: var(--space-3);
}
.loop-step {
  flex: 1;
  background: var(--bg-card);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  padding: var(--space-6);
  transition: border-color var(--transition);
}
.loop-step:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
.loop-step-icon {
  width: 44px;
  height: 44px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--accent-dim);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  color: var(--accent);
  margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
}
.loop-step-num { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
.loop-step-title { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
.loop-step-body { font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; }
.loop-step-body code { font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.8em; }
.loop-arrow {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  padding-top: 54px;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  flex-shrink: 0;
}

/* Confidence */
.confidence-inner {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  gap: var(--space-16);
  align-items: start;
}
.confidence-text { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-4); }
.manifest-body { padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-6); }
.manifest-body pre { font-size: 0.8rem; line-height: 1.8; white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-all; }
.source-legend {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  gap: var(--space-3);
  margin-top: var(--space-4);
}
.legend-item { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-2); font-size: 0.8rem; }
.legend-dot { width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; flex-shrink: 0; }
.legend-dot.direct  { background: #3fb950; }
.legend-dot.elf     { background: #e3b341; }
.legend-dot.runtime { background: #79c0ff; }
.legend-dot.manual  { background: #8b949e; }
.legend-label { color: var(--accent); margin-right: var(--space-1); }
.legend-desc { color: var(--text-muted); }

/* Compare */
.compare-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  gap: var(--space-6);
  align-items: start;
}
.compare-col {
  background: var(--bg-card);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  padding: var(--space-8);
  display: flex;
